{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline","id":189183,"title":"The Tzimisce - a Ventrue Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-05T21:55:32-07:00","id":189183,"title":"The Tzimisce - a Ventrue Bloodline","content":"So I've basically finished the write-up for these guys, I'm editing this first post to reflect that a lot of the issues I had at the start are no longer applicable. So for those interested in the Tzimisce as control freak, flesh-sculpting occultists, here you go:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xOMt97RWoUj_luOD-cYO-shd-cgMgoZ9NtXo5TuG-VM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodline: Tzimisce</a><br /> <br /> I'm using the version of Vicissitude that NeoTiamat created for his <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/63154-walking-shadows-nagloper-vicissitude\">Nagloper write-up</a> (special thanks to him and Charlaquin for that!) and I've decided to make their Gift reflect around controlling their Ghouls. The <i>Szlachta </i>are enhanced by the Privileges to make them better Ghouls, but the Tzimisce also gain the benefit of being able to keep track of them through blood sympathy. They also get a <i>hefty </i>bonus to flesh-sculpting their ghouls, so Tzimisce Ghouls are a thing to fear.<br /> <br /> To explain some of my thought process here, I'm working with an eye towards NeoTiamat's Nagloper write-up, which already includes a weakness that's similar to the original Tzimisce one. I really like his reasoning for it, and I was looking for ways to differentiate the Tzimisce from the Nagloper.<br /> <br /> I was also doing research and found out that the supposed reason the Tzimisce have this weakness is because of Kupala. Seeing as there is no Kupala and no <i>koldun </i>(yet?) I felt like it was an unnecessary bit for the Bloodline. I thought it would be nice to focus on my favored parts of the Tzimisce, those being fleshcrafting and the occult. They're further differentiated by not having a particularly strong tie to the home of the line. They've moved before and they've now moved again.<br /> <br /> I'd definitely be interested in seeing a Bloodline which might go the direction of the Old Clan Tzimisce, too, though I'd probably make them not share a history with the Tzimisce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-10-2014, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T03:44:43-07:00","id":189301,"title":"","content":"Potential Weakness: Soft ban them from staying in the same place for too long. Think Promethean's wasteland, but specifically interfering with their feeding. Some cumulative penalty, reset when they change locations. Give a definition of place that is broad enough that they have to search for somewhere new every night, but narrow enough that they can participated in a chronicle set in a city. Potential penalties include: all actions, feeding, spending extra blood to awaken. Torpor shouldn't let the penalty stack too far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T03:57:24-07:00","id":189305,"title":"","content":"I like it - although not had the chance to go over their Bloodline Gift with a fine comb.<br /> <br /> Personally I like the background and theme, but I always envisaged a Tzimisce bloodline as an offshoot of Gangrel - just because I feel there's no reason why Gangrel can't be Lords (especially a bloodline of Gangrel), and that Dracula has always screamed Gangrel to me - especially with the revised revisions of Protean in Blood &amp; Smoke, which now are pretty much perfect - with perhaps Vicissitude type powers as a great offshoot of Protean. Although it's not just about &quot;powers&quot; that make me think of the Gangrel clan. I might possibly want to use Gangrel with the option of Dominate rather than Ventrue with the option of Protean.<br /> <br /> But please keep working on it! - I might steal it and change the parent clan as just personal preference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T04:24:13-07:00","id":189310,"title":"","content":"Now, I'm not a fan of Masquerade. Never played it. So, I'm coming at this as someone who's only heard about this through the grapevine. <br /> <br /> The Tzim in Masquerade were an ecclesiastic mix of themes and powers to fit their particular backstory. They were fleshy horrors, wearing the beast on in their skin like the Nosferatu are. No, they're eastern europe's Ventrue cousins. No, they were an alternate gangrel style shifter. No, they're... the list goes on. That's a lot of mixed things that won't translate well over into a single bloodline, because, as a clan, they needed to allow to cover a wide range of concepts you can fill in as a character. Bloodlines, however, are the distillation of a single clan concept.<br /> <br /> You are all over the place with things. Your theme is &quot;feudal lords&quot; but you give them shapeshifting powers and note that they're primarily Ordo, who tend to not get involved with the whole neo-feudal structure. They search out scholars - notably people who aren't known for ruling over others, but for study. <br /> <br /> Your blood magic, the whole raison d'etre of the bloodline, is heavily tied to medicine, which again is a very small subset of specialists - that's something that would make good doctors or nurses or even back room drug making biochemists. This lends itself less to scholars or feudal lords again. I really think you need to tighten down the concepts here first priority, then work on the weakness.<br /> <br /> Speaking of magic.... your write up is basically giving the Tzim two new bloodline powers. First, they get protean, and THEN a blood sorcery. I would recommend either eliminating protean, or leaving Protean and making new Obtenebration style devotions to do what you want. Or make bloodline-specific scales that use Protean instead of a Coil as its base. If you are going to keep the blood magic stuff.... then I suggest either deciding if you are going to be allowing Themes or not. Because you're making reference to Hanging Spells which is only possible via Themes. Either make it a special exception to how this blood magic works, and explain how Hanging Spells will work for this stuff, or take a long look at all the other things that the Themes will allow. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T07:42:19-07:00","id":189388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189310#post189310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I'm not a fan of Masquerade. Never played it. So, I'm coming at this as someone who's only heard about this through the grapevine.<br /> <br /> The Tzim in Masquerade were an ecclesiastic mix of themes and powers to fit their particular backstory. They were fleshy horrors, wearing the beast on in their skin like the Nosferatu are. No, they're eastern europe's Ventrue cousins. No, they were an alternate gangrel style shifter. No, they're... the list goes on. That's a lot of mixed things that won't translate well over into a single bloodline, because, as a clan, they needed to allow to cover a wide range of concepts you can fill in as a character. Bloodlines, however, are the distillation of a single clan concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I need to revise the written materials to more accurately reflect that distilled concept. This version of the Tzimisce are Lords without lands. Instead of ruling castles and earth, they rule the very bodies of their servants through Vicissitude. That's the focus of their concept within clan Ventrue, and why I chose the Ventrue over another group like the Gangrel. So with my making that explicit here, does that make sense as a refined concept for the Bloodline? Because that's where I'm operating from.<br /> <br /> Like I said in my original post, I'm willing to dummy out the parts of the Clan from Masquerade that don't quite make sense in the context/aren't as thematically unified. The thing I'm seeing is that the Transcendentalism unifies with the Ordo and Vicissitude as a tool of it, so we can keep that.<br /> <br /> I could also go the opposite direction and suggest that on the whole, the Bloodline is too venal and controlling for the Ordo. Despite their founder's claims of having worked with Dracula, the fact that their desires are so externally focused means they're not really cut out for the Ordo's philosophy, even if their Sorcery is of interest to the Ordo.<br /> <br /> If that were the case, than there could be tensions between the two over the centuries, as the Tzimisce rule a bunch of domains in the Ordo's homeland and make claims of some kind of heritage with Dracula that puts them at odds with the Ordo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189310#post189310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are all over the place with things. Your theme is &quot;feudal lords&quot; but you give them shapeshifting powers and note that they're primarily Ordo, who tend to not get involved with the whole neo-feudal structure. They search out scholars - notably people who aren't known for ruling over others, but for study.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, now I'm really worried, because it somehow failed to come across that despite being in the Ordo, they <i>are </i>interested in politics. I think it's unfair to suggest that one isn't allowed to care about politics in the Ordo. They go against the grain in that regard, which I think is fair, since that seems like a typical subversion of your average Ordo member anyway that people go for, nevermind the fact that none of the Covenants are so rigid that you can't go against the grain on stuff that they don't expressly forbid. If you can have Lancea et Sanctum members who disagree on the religious approach to God &amp;^ Longinus, I'm sure you can have people in the Ordo who elect to pursue politics.<br /> <br /> So the feudal lords thing is their interest. If we have to go back and write more explicit reasoning for it, than I imagine they rationalize it along the lines of seeing their fellows and saying, &quot;Well, <i>somebody </i>has to do it, and we're pretty well suited to it, we think so anyway...&quot;<br /> <br /> Their relationship with the Ordo is both intended to serve as a reference to the Path of Metamorphosis in Old World of Darkness, <i>and </i>because the nature of Vicissitude as a Blood Sorcery would attract the interest of the Ordo. Altering the bodies of the Kindred to make them better predators and whatnot. So we have that reasoning for Ordo interest, and the history in the region of the Ordo's birth and the connection with their inspiration that provides the incentive.<br /> <br /> I think I'll revise the theme a bit. I guess it's better to call them Landless Lords or Lords of Bodies. I'm also reconsidering their connection to the Ordo, though I stand by the notion that it isn't actually heretical or super problematic for a Dragon to decide to be political, unless they've been explicitly instructed not to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189310#post189310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your blood magic, the whole raison d'etre of the bloodline, is heavily tied to medicine, which again is a very small subset of specialists - that's something that would make good doctors or nurses or even back room drug making biochemists. This lends itself less to scholars or feudal lords again. I really think you need to tighten down the concepts here first priority, then work on the weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Medicine is the skill used for control over the bodies of others. It's not necessarily about being a doctor. It's about knowing enough about the body to rule it with their magic. I might use Streetwise in a version of Gilded Cage, but that doesn't mean the Bloodline is all of a sudden about tattoo-wearing, black market-seeking thugs and the like. Lord Tzimisces was well-educated like his contemporary, and the Vicissitude that they stole may have been refined and utilized through scholarly education on the body. If we really have to get that in depth. If you don't like that, swap it with another Mental Skill, like Crafts or Occult. I was gonna make Merits to do that, but whatever works best.<br /> <br /> Not everyone who joins the Bloodline will immediately be good at their Blood Sorcery. In all likelihood, their sires might have to educate them, which puts more emphasis on the mentor-mentee relationship that they have. A Tzimisce is probably mentored by his sire for years before he gets good at Vicissitude, even if you were a doctor, since it's definitely a different means of interacting with the body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189310#post189310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of magic.... your write up is basically giving the Tzim two new bloodline powers. First, they get protean, and THEN a blood sorcery. I would recommend either eliminating protean, or leaving Protean and making new Obtenebration style devotions to do what you want. Or make bloodline-specific scales that use Protean instead of a Coil as its base. If you are going to keep the blood magic stuff.... then I suggest either deciding if you are going to be allowing Themes or not. Because you're making reference to Hanging Spells which is only possible via Themes. Either make it a special exception to how this blood magic works, and explain how Hanging Spells will work for this stuff, or take a long look at all the other things that the Themes will allow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every B&amp;S Bloodline so far has gotten 4 Bloodline Disciplines as a rule, and a Gift. The Gift examples have been an innate, automatic power, Devotions and a Merit Tree so far. Prior to <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i>, some of those Bloodlines who came packaged with a Blood Sorcery <i>also </i>got a Fourth Discipline. The <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Iltani got </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Animalism, Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate <i>and</i> Merges Sorcery. So it seems to me not unreasonable to infer that one could make a Bloodline Blood Sorcery into the Bloodline Gift.<br /> <br /> I looked into it though and noticed some of the others instead took the Bloodline Sorcery as their 4th Discipline, so I'm a little on the fence about it. If push came to shove, I'd ditch the Protean, because it goes less towards that theme of dominating other things mind &amp; body than the rest of their powerset. So I could go either way on that.<br /> <br /> Sorry about the Hanging Spell stuff. It's because I'm using NeoTiamat's version of Vicissitude, which operates off <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/56793-walking-shadows-more-cruac-theban-sorcery-rituals\">slightly altered rules</a>. (refer to Spell Mechanisms) It isn't a reference to Sacraments &amp; Blasphemies necessarily, but I'll make a note in the document to refer to his Blood Sorcery changes, like he does in his original Nagloper writeup. Vicissitude doesn't use the Themes Mechanic in this version.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-06-2014, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T08:05:58-07:00","id":189434,"title":"","content":"Well now. This is flattering. Looks solid overall, though could use tightening, yes. Miscellaneous thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) Theme is key and should inform all other things. I think Lords without Lands is solid, though I also think that it can be refined further. I rather like the idea of the Tzimisce as the ultimate control freaks, using Dominate to take over your mind and Vicissitude to take over your body.<br /> <br /> 2) Obviously, I think the Discipline and Bloodline Sorcery is fine, but then I would. Medicine is there for the purely practical reason that if you are going to be warping flesh and bone, you should know how not to accidentally impale your ghoul's spleen with a bone spike in the process, which requires knowing where the spleen is. <br /> <br /> 3) I <i>would</i> be careful about tying the Tzimisce and the Ordo Dracul too tightly together. That is to say, while there's a definite historical connection, I'd also make it clearer that the Tzimisce can and do go hang out in other Covenants. The Invictus is an obvious choice, the Crone is quite plausible. One of the more irritating habits, I think, of earlier VtR Bloodlines was to treat them as though every bloodline member meets the stereotype of the clan and joins the same covenant. <br /> <br /> 4) As far as weakness goes... perhaps look to the Bron Weakness, from one of the early Bloodlines books (Legendary, I think it was?). The idea is that whenever the Tzimisce is in <i>charge</i> of something, they take a (10-Humanity or 10-Humanity/2) penalty to rolls related to maintaining and using that power. Make that powerful and eloquent Tzimisce the Prince, and all of a sudden, they start tripping over their tongue. A Tzimisce becomes a mentor to a younger student, and their minds cloud up whenever they're trying to explain the Coils. <br /> <br /> How to explain it / justify it? Well, at least with the Nagloper, I had the idea that Vicissitude is taught, first of all, by the Strix. The Tzimisce appear to have gotten on the bad side of the Strix in a bad way, and they claim to have stolen Vicissitude, so... perhaps a curse?<br /> <br /> In any case, the weakness is both markedly painful if you are trying to rise high in the ranks, and also <i>very aggravating</i>. It makes people with an extremely strong sense of ego into making the choice between being a follower and being constantly sabotaged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T08:20:58-07:00","id":189444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189434#post189434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well now. This is flattering. Looks solid overall, though could use tightening, yes. Miscellaneous thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1) Theme is key and should inform all other things. I think Lords without Lands is solid, though I also think that it can be refined further. I rather like the idea of the Tzimisce as the ultimate control freaks, using Dominate to take over your mind and Vicissitude to take over your body.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like the notion of Control Freaks. It would probably inform them better, so I'm gonna operate with that in mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189434#post189434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Obviously, I think the Discipline and Bloodline Sorcery is fine, but then I would. Medicine is there for the purely practical reason that if you are going to be warping flesh and bone, you should know how not to accidentally impale your ghoul's spleen with a bone spike in the process, which requires knowing where the spleen is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189434#post189434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) I <i>would</i> be careful about tying the Tzimisce and the Ordo Dracul too tightly together. That is to say, while there's a definite historical connection, I'd also make it clearer that the Tzimisce can and do go hang out in other Covenants. The Invictus is an obvious choice, the Crone is quite plausible. One of the more irritating habits, I think, of earlier VtR Bloodlines was to treat them as though every bloodline member meets the stereotype of the clan and joins the same covenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more and more thinking I might go with a version where the story told of Tzimisces is apocryphal at best and an outright lie at its worst. He might've stolen Vicissitude all on his own and claimed that Dracula helped him after the fact. It might cleave to the theme a bit more if he's claiming that Dracula was the helper rather than the other way around, which might rub the Ordo the wrong way. I'm not sure if it would post-Blood &amp; Smoke though, since they were <i>inspired </i>by him and they seem to not be the sorts that waste time getting personally offended by people claiming things like that.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's specifically an issue with the Ordo of the Carpathians.<br /> <br /> Perhaps Tzimisces didn't steal Vicissitude at all, but rather made a deal with a Strix in which he claimed he would deliver them the Carpathians. It seemed like a good idea at the time! But then he winds up with a very temporary Voivodate. Maybe he becomes the control freak through paranoia about the Strix, and his line is supernaturally cursed with that same fear. Or it just might be flavor that informs their behavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189434#post189434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 4) As far as weakness goes... perhaps look to the Bron Weakness, from one of the early Bloodlines books (Legendary, I think it was?). The idea is that whenever the Tzimisce is in <i>charge</i> of something, they take a (10-Humanity or 10-Humanity/2) penalty to rolls related to maintaining and using that power. Make that powerful and eloquent Tzimisce the Prince, and all of a sudden, they start tripping over their tongue. A Tzimisce becomes a mentor to a younger student, and their minds cloud up whenever they're trying to explain the Coils.<br /> <br /> How to explain it / justify it? Well, at least with the Nagloper, I had the idea that Vicissitude is taught, first of all, by the Strix. The Tzimisce appear to have gotten on the bad side of the Strix in a bad way, and they claim to have stolen Vicissitude, so... perhaps a curse?<br /> <br /> In any case, the weakness is both markedly painful if you are trying to rise high in the ranks, and also <i>very aggravating</i>. It makes people with an extremely strong sense of ego into making the choice between being a follower and being constantly sabotaged.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it, but at the same time, I would like something which ties into the Bloodline Gift of Vicissitude. Maybe they lose their nerve easily when they screw up. Failing a roll to control others through Animalism or Dominate might suspend access to Vicissitude for the scene, as the Tzimisce becomes angry at their inability to control and is unable to muster up the power. Good old fashioned impotence.<br /> <br /> Gonna think on this some.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T08:45:58-07:00","id":189454,"title":"","content":"I think that generally cloaking the Tzimisce origins in myth and legend is a good idea. Basically, lay out what the common <i>story</i> is, but how true it is, and how people react to it, is a different matter.<br /> <br /> Weakness... well, something that makes them more Strix-y? Look at the Strix Banes? Might give them glowy reflective eyes as an additional mini-weakness, just for freaking people out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T12:25:22-07:00","id":189552,"title":"","content":"Re-written just about everything except for a Bloodline Bane. Still working on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:27:58-07:00","id":189603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189388#post189388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I need to revise the written materials to more accurately reflect that distilled concept. This version of the Tzimisce are Lords without lands. Instead of ruling castles and earth, they rule the very bodies of their servants through Vicissitude. That's the focus of their concept within clan Ventrue, and why I chose the Ventrue over another group like the Gangrel. So with my making that explicit here, does that make sense as a refined concept for the Bloodline? Because that's where I'm operating from.</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering that &quot;lords without land&quot; doesn't mean much to me, I have no idea what you're saying. Without land implies you don't have territory or a people, but then you go on to talk about controlling people? <br /> <br /> Notable is that Animalism also provides territory-land control powers. So, if you're going to be &quot;Lords without Land,&quot; but have land control powers? Something is jinky there. And what happens if one of your Tzim went Circle and learned their territory control rites?<br /> <br /> There's a lot of conflict here from what I feel. Perhaps it would be better to focus on &quot;master of human/animal pets&quot; instead of the land thing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like I said in my original post, I'm willing to dummy out the parts of the Clan from Masquerade that don't quite make sense in the context/aren't as thematically unified. The thing I'm seeing is that the Transcendentalism unifies with the Ordo and Vicissitude as a tool of it, so we can keep that.<br /> <br /> I could also go the opposite direction and suggest that on the whole, the Bloodline is too venal and controlling for the Ordo. Despite their founder's claims of having worked with Dracula, the fact that their desires are so externally focused means they're not really cut out for the Ordo's philosophy, even if their Sorcery is of interest to the Ordo. </div> </div> </div> The Ordo Dracul is the bastard love children of Tzim and Tremere philosophies. Even if you go to the whole &quot;too extreme, they're cast out!&quot; thing, you're going to still be heavily influenced by Ordo philosophies. It might not be the first time a bloodline wasn't allowed part of a main covenant because &quot;heresy!!!&quot; but often that's because of story reasons. Go with what fits your (or the vast majority) of stories.<br /> <br /> That said, you should consider that, even if the majority do join the Ordo, there will be a number who go towards other Covenants. The Embrace doesn't determine philosophy, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Man, now I'm really worried, because it somehow failed to come across that despite being in the Ordo, they <i>are </i>interested in politics. I think it's unfair to suggest that one isn't allowed to care about politics in the Ordo. They go against the grain in that regard, which I think is fair, since that seems like a typical subversion of your average Ordo member anyway that people go for, nevermind the fact that none of the Covenants are so rigid that you can't go against the grain on stuff that they don't expressly forbid. If you can have Lancea et Sanctum members who disagree on the religious approach to God &amp;^ Longinus, I'm sure you can have people in the Ordo who elect to pursue politics. </div> </div> </div> One word: Why?<br /> <br /> Why are they interested in politics? You say they are. But being recruited from scholars, being inducted into a field of controlling people... where's all the politics coming from? Why? <br /> <br /> I feel like you're telling any potentials to be interested, but not having any -reason- to be. Think about it this way - lets say that I'm a scholar of some kind, say the history of World War II. A Tzim decides to embrace me for some reason. I'm inducted into the bloodline. I'm inducted into the Ordo Dracul. Why am I suddenly interested in engaging in politics beyond what the character background and covenant suggest? <br /> <br /> Ordo ventrue are as likely to become Axe or Dying Light Sworn as anything else. So, why emphasis? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the feudal lords thing is their interest. If we have to go back and write more explicit reasoning for it, than I imagine they rationalize it along the lines of seeing their fellows and saying, &quot;Well, <i>somebody </i>has to do it, and we're pretty well suited to it, we think so anyway...&quot; </div> </div> </div> That... is a pretty weak reason. There's already the Sworn of the Mysteries who fill that role. You don't need a bloodline for it. As well, why is there no interest in the Invictus, the actual feudal structure of the vampire world? <br /> <br /> And how are they well suited? Because they have Dominate? Auspex, Majesty, Nightmare are all equally suited to political shenanigans, let alone just actual skills (which, if we're being recruited from scholars, I have to ask where these skills are coming from). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their relationship with the Ordo is both intended to serve as a reference to the Path of Metamorphosis in Old World of Darkness, <i>and </i>because the nature of Vicissitude as a Blood Sorcery would attract the interest of the Ordo. Altering the bodies of the Kindred to make them better predators and whatnot. So we have that reasoning for Ordo interest, and the history in the region of the Ordo's birth and the connection with their inspiration that provides the incentive. </div> </div> </div> Provides an incentive to join the Ordo, perhaps. Not seeing how it influences anything else.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Medicine is the skill used for control over the bodies of others. It's not necessarily about being a doctor. It's about knowing enough about the body to rule it with their magic. </div> </div> </div> And where do they learn medicine? They'll have to take classes for medical doctors, nursing, biochemistry, or the like. They will have to learn about anatomy. <br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum are big into Academics. They support huge libraries, they encourage study and philosophy. The Circle are occulists, spreading information through their contacts and mentors and friends, all working it in a wide, ecclesiastic circle of knowledge. The magic skill has a lot of support from the covenants to encourage its growth. <br /> <br /> What does the bloodline do to encourage the teaching of medicine? You may not be a doctor, but you ARE going to be studying the same things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not everyone who joins the Bloodline will immediately be good at their Blood Sorcery. In all likelihood, their sires might have to educate them, which puts more emphasis on the mentor-mentee relationship that they have. A Tzimisce is probably mentored by his sire for years before he gets good at Vicissitude, even if you were a doctor, since it's definitely a different means of interacting with the body. </div> </div> </div> This is what I mean by being scattershot and unfocused themes. Because now you're just suggesting that you are going to have another area you have to study into.<br /> <br /> Start off as a scholar. <br /> Learn to play politics.<br /> Study medicine so you can use magic.<br /> <br /> You're pulling the character concepts in several different ways now. It seems to me that you are also saying that its unlikely that someone freshly embraced won't be able to fill the bloodline's concept from character creation. Which is something I feel that is problematic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Every B&amp;S Bloodline so far has gotten 4 Bloodline Disciplines as a rule, and a Gift. </div> </div> </div> ..... Neglectu don't get a fourth discipline. They only get a gift, and only one related to making revenants. I've heard that future bloodlines won't necessarily get a fourth discipline. So, not quite a rule.<br /> <br /> Khaibit get a low level ability that's enhancing natural Kindred senses AND access to devotions. Cerberus get a bonus to pursuing Conditions AND a merit that enhances another innate ability of Kindred. <br /> <br /> Gifts are something that's automatic to work the bloodline's concept. You get them immediately, and maybe something you can buy up a bit later. Simply dropping access to a blood magic isn't quite the same. Especially a blood magic you just admitted that someone inducted into the bloodline won't be able to use until after being tutored. That seems to be going against the nature of the gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Gift examples have been an innate, automatic power, Devotions and a Merit Tree so far. Prior to <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i>, some of those Bloodlines who came packaged with a Blood Sorcery <i>also </i>got a Fourth Discipline. The <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Iltani got </span></span>[COLOR=#000000][FONT=arial]Animalism, Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate <i>and</i> Merges Sorcery. So it seems to me not unreasonable to infer that one could make a Bloodline Blood Sorcery into the Bloodline Gift. </div> </div> </div> Merges Sorcery was tied to a historical organization, not the bloodline. The two weren't mutually inclusive; you could take Merges without the bloodline. You could be in the bloodline without Merges.<br /> <br /> The Vedma bloodline taught the Ordo Dracul the discipline Spoiling and blood alchemy devotions. However, this &quot;magic&quot; they shared wasn't tied into the bloodline, but like Merges, open to anyone to learn.<br /> <br /> By associating it with the bloodline directly as a Gift, however, you are making it unable to be accessed by anyone outside the bloodline. Given the close association your bloodline has with the Ordo, its unlikely that such a sorcery would remain unique to the bloodline without some aspect keeping it under wraps, by simple virtue of scholastic theft. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T13:33:22-07:00","id":189608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189603#post189603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One word: Why?<br /> <br /> Why are they interested in politics? You say they are. But being recruited from scholars, being inducted into a field of controlling people... where's all the politics coming from? Why?<br /> <br /> I feel like you're telling any potentials to be interested, but not having any -reason- to be. Think about it this way - lets say that I'm a scholar of some kind, say the history of World War II. A Tzim decides to embrace me for some reason. I'm inducted into the bloodline. I'm inducted into the Ordo Dracul. Why am I suddenly interested in engaging in politics beyond what the character background and covenant suggest?<br /> <br /> Ordo ventrue are as likely to become Axe or Dying Light Sworn as anything else. So, why emphasis?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're already recruiting people who are interested in being the Manager or the Department Head or the General. So all they're really doing is saying, &quot;The Domain is now your Department, use your drive to excel.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189603#post189603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That... is a pretty weak reason. There's already the Sworn of the Mysteries who fill that role. You don't need a bloodline for it. As well, why is there no interest in the Invictus, the actual feudal structure of the vampire world?</div> </div> </div> </div>The latest version doesn't really associate them with the Ordo. They might enjoy the hierarchy focused nature of the Invictus, but the fondness for the Masquerade and Vicissitude's vulgar nature might make that hard to balance. I'd definitely say there are members that are Invictus, but depending on the city, they might run into challenges on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189603#post189603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how are they well suited? Because they have Dominate? Auspex, Majesty, Nightmare are all equally suited to political shenanigans, let alone just actual skills (which, if we're being recruited from scholars, I have to ask where these skills are coming from).</div> </div> </div> </div>They think they're well suited to controlling people because they can control their minds and their bodies, so they're trying for positions which give them plenty of bodies to control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189603#post189603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And where do they learn medicine? They'll have to take classes for medical doctors, nursing, biochemistry, or the like. They will have to learn about anatomy.<br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum are big into Academics. They support huge libraries, they encourage study and philosophy. The Circle are occulists, spreading information through their contacts and mentors and friends, all working it in a wide, ecclesiastic circle of knowledge. The magic skill has a lot of support from the covenants to encourage its growth.<br /> <br /> What does the bloodline do to encourage the teaching of medicine? You may not be a doctor, but you ARE going to be studying the same things.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThese are all good points that I'm trying to work through.<br /> <br /> What do you think of Crafts instead of Medicine? Think imposing one's will onto another like a sculptor might impose his will on marble to make a statue. Or a painter on the canvas, etcetera. The original elders of the bloodline were recruited from ambitious nobility who in all likelihood received an education in art. Vicissitude being an applied art of dominating someone else's body like your preferred medium.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189603#post189603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">..... Neglatu don't get a fourth discipline. They only get a gift, and only one related to making revenants. I've heard that future bloodlines won't necessarily get a fourth discipline. So, not quite a rule.<br /> <br /> Khaibit get a low level ability that's enhancing natural Kindred senses AND access to devotions. Cerberus get a bonus to pursuing Conditions AND a merit that enhances another innate ability of Kindred.<br /> <br /> Gifts are something that's automatic to work the bloodline's concept. You get them immediately, and maybe something you can buy up a bit later. Simply dropping access to a blood magic isn't quite the same. Especially a blood magic you just admitted that someone inducted into the bloodline won't be able to use until after being tutored. That seems to be going against the nature of the gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, Rose did say she wanted to give the Neglatu Resilience, but didn't for fear of shortchanging Ventrue/Gangrel members of the Neglatu. So I think there's a certain desire to stick to that, but I doubt they want to paint themselves into a corner by making a hard &amp; fast rule about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189603#post189603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Merges Sorcery was tied to a historical organization, not the bloodline. The two weren't mutually inclusive; you could take Merges without the bloodline. You could be in the bloodline without Merges.<br /> <br /> The Vedma bloodline taught the Ordo Dracul the discipline Spoiling and blood alchemy devotions. However, this &quot;magic&quot; they shared wasn't tied into the bloodline, but like Merges, open to anyone to learn.<br /> <br /> By associating it with the bloodline directly as a Gift, however, you are making it unable to be accessed by anyone outside the bloodline. Given the close association your bloodline has with the Ordo, its unlikely that such a sorcery would remain unique to the bloodline without some aspect keeping it under wraps, by simple virtue of scholastic theft.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess a better comparison might be with the Architects of the Monolith, who get Gilded Cage as a proprietary blood sorcery. Notably they also don't get a 4th discipline, they instead replace one of their existing disciplines with Auspex. So that's something I've got to think on.<br /> <br /> If Vicissitude instead becomes the fourth Discipline of the Tzimisce, that'll leave them without a Gift for the moment. Not necessarily a problem, but I'm not entirely sure what to give them.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> While I get the sense you're not a fan of Vicissitude, for argument's sake if you had to have it, what Attribute + Skill would you give it to? I'm getting a sense that you don't like Medicine, but not what you'd prefer. Your &quot;master of human/animal pets&quot; description seems adequate for them. They can control your mind with Dominate and Animalism, and they can control your body with Vicissitude. Total domination of another being. That's what Vicissitude means for them.<br /> <br /> The ability to do so combined with the founder's desire to be a ruler instills the bloodline with that ambition. Not magically, but by virtue of who was selected to join. During its early nights, it was the gentry that wanted or had land in the domain. In modern nights, they might pick anyone who shows a similar ambition to lead in their chosen field. I suppose that ambition is the real key.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, being a leader in any field also involves a certain amount of politics. The head of the History Department isn't doing exactly what the State Senator is doing, but their job involves working people and playing internal politics and the like to get ahead. People that are in leadership positions in a variety of different fields aren't always there because they're literally the best at the general job, but because they're good at both the job and networking. If you got to the position solely through seniority and the like, than you're probably lacking the ambition that they're usually going for. They want the banker that closes deals <i>and </i>tries to schmooze his boss for the promotion, because he's demonstrating the initiative to show he wants power. You don't need to change anything really to get the department head at the university, or the iconoclastic artist, the new head surgeon or the newest leader on the fireteam.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?<br /> <br /> Stressing that this is an iterative process. What works stays, what doesn't goes, until it gets to the point where it feels more or less put together.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Reflecting on this more, the central theme I'm working with at the moment is that they're control freaks, and it's expressed through controlling bodies and minds. The desire for control and the desire for leadership positions aren't necessarily the same thing. So that's something I'm reflecting on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-06-2014, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T15:42:04-07:00","id":189679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189608#post189608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're already recruiting people who are interested in being the Manager or the Department Head or the General. So all they're really doing is saying, &quot;The Domain is now your Department, use your drive to excel.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> You've suggested &quot;ambitious minds&quot; which is not the same thing as recruiting managers, or the like. And it feels really odd to me to have someone like that recruited. Forced. Ventrue blood does tend to inspire arrogance and ambition and, most notably, detachment from others. But it doesn't push them towards embracing ambition in very specific fields. <br /> <br /> Like, I'm imagining a Tzim giving the Embrace to a particular favored subject he's been playing with. Or how about someone that Embraces a research assistance, specifically chosen to not have ambition (which could be a threat to himself). Its too easy to deviate from the &quot;only turn XY people into vampires.&quot; And, once you do, then the grand-childer will also likely be off that &quot;chosen people&quot; pool.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend some kind of bloodline flaw or weakness if you felt it truly necessary to enforce it. Something akin to how the ventrue are detached from people by nature, but the Tzim feel more detached, or can't relate to, people they haven't used an affinity power on? Something like that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They think they're well suited to controlling people because they can control their minds and their bodies, so they're trying for positions which give them plenty of bodies to control. </div> </div> </div> Bodies to manipulate would recommend having herds or retainers; one could simply start abducting people off the street, or from colleges, or whatever, dominate / blood bond them into serving you. If anything, their magics would push them towards picking on fringe people, and not those more likely to be noticed missing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bThese are all good points that I'm trying to work through.<br /> <br /> What do you think of Crafts instead of Medicine? Think imposing one's will onto another like a sculptor might impose his will on marble to make a statue. Or a painter on the canvas, etcetera. The original elders of the bloodline were recruited from ambitious nobility who in all likelihood received an education in art. Vicissitude being an applied art of dominating someone else's body like your preferred medium. </div> </div> </div> Its not the skill that I have an issue with, its how its related to what I see as conflicting concepts in the bloodline. &quot;Lords without Lands&quot; or politicians or the like are very unlikely to have developed those areas, and entering that field of study, and all the supporting skills and resources they need to develop, feel like they're pulling in two different directions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Incidentally, Rose did say she wanted to give the Neglatu Resilience, but didn't for fear of shortchanging Ventrue/Gangrel members of the Neglatu. So I think there's a certain desire to stick to that, but I doubt they want to paint themselves into a corner by making a hard &amp; fast rule about it. </div> </div> </div> I didn't hear that before. Huh.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Vicissitude instead becomes the fourth Discipline of the Tzimisce, that'll leave them without a Gift for the moment. Not necessarily a problem, but I'm not entirely sure what to give them. </div> </div> </div> Mmm.... my thoughts on the issue below.<br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While I get the sense you're not a fan of Vicissitude, for argument's sake if you had to have it, what Attribute + Skill would you give it to? I'm getting a sense that you don't like Medicine, but not what you'd prefer. Your &quot;master of human/animal pets&quot; description seems adequate for them. They can control your mind with Dominate and Animalism, and they can control your body with Vicissitude. Total domination of another being. That's what Vicissitude means for them. </div> </div> </div> I was actually good with Int + Medicine. My concern is that mechanics of the bloodline feel like they're lending themselves to a different direction than what your concept and history are suggesting. That's the conflict.<br /> <br /> Also, I did say that I never played Masquerade. I'm really not invested in liking or disliking Vicissitude. Nor in recreating something from Masquerade, of which I've only heard third hand stories. I'm just trying to give feedback on the overall feel of the bloodline, and I just feel like there's a conflict of themes here.<br /> <br /> I mean, just based on the idea of Vicissitude, my first thought was actually to jump to &quot;Carthian Doctor&quot; and take it to an extreme. My second thought was that it felt like an alternative Protean, and the bloodline gift could be to alter the discipline as they learn it - earning different powers for each level, and how they can apply it to others. Simply make learning Protean 1 a requirement for joining the bloodline, kind of like how being revenant is part of the Neglectu requirements.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ability to do so combined with the founder's desire to be a ruler instills the bloodline with that ambition. Not magically, but by virtue of who was selected to join. During its early nights, it was the gentry that wanted or had land in the domain. In modern nights, they might pick anyone who shows a similar ambition to lead in their chosen field. I suppose that ambition is the real key.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, being a leader in any field also involves a certain amount of politics. The head of the History Department isn't doing exactly what the State Senator is doing, but their job involves working people and playing internal politics and the like to get ahead. People that are in leadership positions in a variety of different fields aren't always there because they're literally the best at the general job, but because they're good at both the job and networking. If you got to the position solely through seniority and the like, than you're probably lacking the ambition that they're usually going for. They want the banker that closes deals <i>and </i>tries to schmooze his boss for the promotion, because he's demonstrating the initiative to show he wants power. You don't need to change anything really to get the department head at the university, or the iconoclastic artist, the new head surgeon or the newest leader on the fireteam.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense? </div> </div> </div> Still feels forced, such that one exception in a scattered bloodline will create an entire branch of non-political Tzim. Especially when the Embrace, being a life altering and traumatic event, is well known for people changing the path of their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-06-2014, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T16:41:19-07:00","id":189696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189679#post189679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You've suggested &quot;ambitious minds&quot; which is not the same thing as recruiting managers, or the like. And it feels really odd to me to have someone like that recruited. Forced. Ventrue blood does tend to inspire arrogance and ambition and, most notably, detachment from others. But it doesn't push them towards embracing ambition in very specific fields.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm imagining a Tzim giving the Embrace to a particular favored subject he's been playing with. Or how about someone that Embraces a research assistance, specifically chosen to not have ambition (which could be a threat to himself). Its too easy to deviate from the &quot;only turn XY people into vampires.&quot; And, once you do, then the grand-childer will also likely be off that &quot;chosen people&quot; pool.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend some kind of bloodline flaw or weakness if you felt it truly necessary to enforce it. Something akin to how the ventrue are detached from people by nature, but the Tzim feel more detached, or can't relate to, people they haven't used an affinity power on? Something like that?<br /> <br /> Bodies to manipulate would recommend having herds or retainers; one could simply start abducting people off the street, or from colleges, or whatever, dominate / blood bond them into serving you. If anything, their magics would push them towards picking on fringe people, and not those more likely to be noticed missing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your point here, particularly for the weakness where they have problems interacting with people they haven't used an affinity power on. I feel that dovetails nicely with a theme of control freaks.<br /> <br /> I think I'm gonna switch gears and go back to the drawing board for the concept. Medicine being important to them feels interesting. Maybe their founder was a court physician or the like. Maybe they tie into ghouls or ghoul families by studying/searching for particular lineages of kine that are able to tolerate more alteration by Vicissitude, and these people with the special genes form the basis for the <i>szlachta</i>. Some of whom they might even Embrace to help with experiments, or because they're subservient or because they're particularly interesting as a subject.<br /> <br /> The Fiend nickname can arise from their experimentation. I imagine you might call the creepy guy who steals people in the night to turn them into monsters some kind of demon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189679#post189679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not the skill that I have an issue with, its how its related to what I see as conflicting concepts in the bloodline. &quot;Lords without Lands&quot; or politicians or the like are very unlikely to have developed those areas, and entering that field of study, and all the supporting skills and resources they need to develop, feel like they're pulling in two different directions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so I'm gonna ditch that route. I like the arrogant control freak scientist angle a bit more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189679#post189679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't hear that before. Huh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll keep hunting for the thread, but it involved a few people on here, and some folks suggesting as a fix that the Neglatu might take any Physical Discipline they don't have, after Rose threw that out. It might've been the one about Physical Disciplines and Requirements. I'll keep looking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189679#post189679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually good with Int + Medicine. My concern is that mechanics of the bloodline feel like they're lending themselves to a different direction than what your concept and history are suggesting. That's the conflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I'm considering the medicine focus more strongly than before, and ditching the focus on their being lords entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189679#post189679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I did say that I never played Masquerade. I'm really not invested in liking or disliking Vicissitude. Nor in recreating something from Masquerade, of which I've only heard third hand stories. I'm just trying to give feedback on the overall feel of the bloodline, and I just feel like there's a conflict of themes here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually really dislike Masquerade, but I have a soft spot for Vicissitude and wanted to see if the idea of the Tzimisce could be rehabilitated into something more interesting. Obviously having mixed results so far, but let's see where we're going.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189679#post189679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, just based on the idea of Vicissitude, my first thought was actually to jump to &quot;Carthian Doctor&quot; and take it to an extreme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funnily enough, that was the character concept that I was thinking of when writing it. I wasn't sure if I should suggest the Carthian angle since the idea at the time was still landless lords.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189679#post189679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My second thought was that it felt like an alternative Protean, and the bloodline gift could be to alter the discipline as they learn it - earning different powers for each level, and how they can apply it to others. Simply make learning Protean 1 a requirement for joining the bloodline, kind of like how being revenant is part of the Neglectu requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm gonna stick with the Blood Sorcery expression of Vicissitude, if nothing else because I prefer the implication that Vicissitude is more learned than instinctive, as opposed to Protean. They each have their benefits, with Vicissitude being a more external and less reactive expression of the Beast, I'm thinking. Which still doesn't solve the Gift problem. What if they get Vicissitude as their 4th Discipline as a Blood Sorcery, and their Gift is the ability to spot people with the potential and turn them into more potent ghouls that accept Vicissitude more easily? Could be that these people become the <i>szlachta </i>and sometimes even potential Embrace candidates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=189679#post189679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still feels forced, such that one exception in a scattered bloodline will create an entire branch of non-political Tzim. Especially when the Embrace, being a life altering and traumatic event, is well known for people changing the path of their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, tossing out the ultra political leader fixation.<br /> <br /> How does all of that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-06T21:46:34-07:00","id":189919,"title":"","content":"I've revised the document again. This time going for the scholar background combined with their being control freaks as the theme. If there's still parts of the write up that feel conflicting or unfocused, please let me know.<br /> <br /> I changed Vicissitude to be their fourth discipline and gave them a Gift. It makes the Ghouls that they create better than normal ghouls, though I'm not totally sure how I feel about it.<br /> <br /> Also included a weakness. The first two paragraphs still need tweaking, but the rest is ready for scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Any additional suggestions on the Gift are appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-08T16:08:49-07:00","id":191766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline#post189183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've been writing up the Bloodline that people didn't really want, the Tzimisce as Ventrue. What I've got so far feels okay, with the problem that I'm unable to think of an interesting weakness that ties into the themes I'm playing with in their write up. To that end, I could use your guy's help.<br /> <br /> I'm gonna post some bits of info and see if we can't assemble information from there.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Here's a link to the full writeup, which is obviously subject to revisions. It'll be cleaned up and tightened in terms of description once I have an idea of the Weakness.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xOMt97RWoUj_luOD-cYO-shd-cgMgoZ9NtXo5TuG-VM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodline: Tzimisce</a><br /> <br /> I'm using the version of Vicissitude that NeoTiamat created for his <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/63154-walking-shadows-nagloper-vicissitude\">Nagloper write-up</a> (special thanks to him and Charlaquin for that!) and treating it as a Bloodline Gift. They get Protean as their Bloodline Discipline, unsurprisingly. Maybe something to do with Vicissitude? It seems like, of the Bloodlines released so far, their weaknesses had to do with their Gifts, more or less. The Neglatu are still Revenant-enough that they can't blood bond. The Khaibit are blinded and unable to use Obtenebration when exposed to too much light. The Kerberos aren't as good at stuff unless they're following up their Predatory Aura, etcetera.<br /> <br /> Any help? If you don't like any of the details given up, I don't mind hearing about that either. I want to make these guys the best that I can. Help me out, people.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To explain some of my thought process here, I'm working with an eye towards NeoTiamat's Nagloper write-up, which already includes a weakness that's similar to the original Tzimisce one. I really like his reasoning for it, and I was looking for ways to differentiate the Tzimisce from the Nagloper.<br /> <br /> I was also doing research and found out that the supposed reason the Tzimisce have this weakness is because of Kupala. Seeing as there is no Kupala and no <i>koldun </i>(yet?) I felt like it was an unnecessary bit for the Bloodline. To help further differentiate them from their peers, I decided to go in the direction of their being landless lords. I don't think it's a representative of their metaphysical condition, but a result of politics. It also explains why the Tzimisce aren't all concentrated and powerful, and why they've dispersed. I thought it might be a nice touch for them to specifically not be in their homelands any longer.<br /> <br /> So that's why I'm trying to find a different weakness for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I been toying with an adaption of old clan as eastern lords with the nos bane plus the home soil bane. Koldunic sorcery is a cruac like form with Transformation as one of the favored themes.<br /> I'll have to rethink that with the gangrel suggestion. A gangrel with dominate? Or a Lord with protean?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Old_Clan_Tzimisce#Old_Clan_Tzimisce\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Old_..._Clan_Tzimisce</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T14:29:13-07:00","id":192759,"title":"","content":"I personally dislike mixing the non-physical disciplines such as Protean into another clan's bloodline. I too think the new Tzimisce should stem from clan Gangrel, largely because the new Protean so very much emulates old Vicissitude on a personal scale and it seams logical that the Tzimisce as a bloodline have learned to use that skill on others. Though I do agree thematically they are more Ventrue than Gangrel, but they wouldn't be the first bloodline with a significantly different theme than it's base clan.<br /> <br /> That said, I very much enjoy this bloodline, I'll certainly add it to my list of those available in my B&amp;S chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","user":"Xaielao","date":". 07-09-2014, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T22:19:26-07:00","id":193159,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of the lordly focus on dominion this version has combined with occult flair. I could easily see a progressive Fiend paying the Carthians or the Ordo lip service in order to slake their Vicissitude needs as a Night Surgeon or Dragon, think The Repo Man from Repo! The Genetic Opera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>\u201cAnd those who were seen dancing were thought to be insane by those who could not hear the music.\u201d - Friedrich Nietzsche</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/812-datura","name":"Datura","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-09T22:49:32-07:00","id":193189,"title":"","content":"Glad you guys are enjoying it. I'm considering writing some additional Merits for anyone interested, as well as some sidebar-esque fluff with recommendations on the origins of Vicissitude as the Tzimisce have it. I think it's better they're presented as optional, additional history that people can use or discard as they like, so the general Bloodline's stuff isn't overly concerned with it.<br /> <br /> When I imagine the Bloodline's occultism, I imagine them researching as often as they send their <i>szlachta </i>to steal research from other occultists and sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Minor Update, added two Alterations that I felt were interesting to the Vicissitude write-up. Reposting them here for ease of access:<br /> <br /> <b>Rank 3 Alterations</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><u>Butchery of the Able Flesh</u></span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Target Number of Successes</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 10</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The flesh-sculptor is able to refine the violent properties of Vicissitude that allow him to mutilate the bodies of others, refining them to focus on specific body parts and damaging them. This Alteration allows the flesh-sculptor to inflict longer term Conditions and Tilts, representing refined strikes against the functional anatomy of the target. The flesh-sculptor may inflict 1 Condition/Tilt initially, and others for every 3 dots of Potency.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Tilts such as Arm Wrack, Leg Wrack, Blindness, and Deafen are often inflicted, and Conditions such as Disabled or Mute may also be applied. This Alteration may be used as a Hanged Spell or can be cast as normal upon a subject of Vicissitude. The ritualist must touch his opponent by making a Dexterity + Brawl roll minus the victim\u2019s Defense in order to activate the Hanged Spell.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Rank 5 Alterations</b><br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><u>Ascendancy of Alacritous Change</u></span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Target Number of Successes</span></b></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: 10</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">By using this Alteration immediately before another Alteration, the subsequent use of Vicissitude is rendered into a Hanging Spell, prepaid for seven days, with a trigger of the flesh-sculptor's touch. Unlike the Gift of the Slumbering Flesh, the Alteration isn\u2019t held dormant in its target, the flesh-sculptor holds it and can inflict it upon a target of their choosing when touching them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This power allows the flesh-sculptor to seemingly inflict instantaneous Alterations that have been prepared, touching them using a Dexterity + Brawl minus the victim\u2019s Defense. Any Alterations which are subject to Ascendancy of Alacritous Change are treated as Hanging Spells and must be extended to keep them after the initial time period is up.</span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What do you guys think? I feel the ideas are solid, but I feel like the mechanics might need tightening. As always, all feedback is appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 07-11-2014, 02:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T14:01:39-07:00","id":194966,"title":"","content":"I like the Rank 3 alteration very much, it makes great use of the condition &amp; tilt systems to represent the old V;tM horror and fear of Tzimisce warping the flesh of their enemies on the battlefield. The Rank 5 Alteration does need a little touching up, perhaps to help diversify it from Gift of Slumbering Flesh. It is potentially extremely powerful as well, with the ability to permanently hobble and opponent with a simple touch attack. Perhaps I'm missing something as I am unfamiliar with 'hanging spells'. I don't own nor have I played M:tAw which I assume that is from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T17:07:01-07:00","id":195115,"title":"","content":"Well, there's two mechanical things to understand:<br /> <br /> Vicissitude isn't permanent. When trying to naturally recover from Vicissitude's Alterations, you treat them as lethal wounds equal to the minimum number of successes required for the Alteration. So for instance with Supplication of the Skin, a human can heal it over time as if it were a 7L wound. It is not an actual 7L wound, but the duration for an unmodified human to heal away Supplication of the Skin would be 14 days, as they heal 1 Lethal damage every 2 days at their natural rate. Ghouls and Kindred can (in the case of Kindred, they have to) spend Vitae to accelerate this process. If I were Kindred and I were afflicted with Supplication of the Skin, I could spend 7 Vitae and heal it immediately.<br /> <br /> Hanging Spells are a mechanic from NeoTiamat's Blood Sorcery rules which makes certain rituals such as the Touch of Morrigan or Mutilate the Earthly Form into Hanging Spells. Once you cast them, they lie dormant until their trigger is activated. They last for 24 hours after you finish casting the ritual. After that, you have to spend 1 Vitae to extend it another 24 hours if you want to hold onto it longer.<br /> <br /> I've reproduced the explanation for Hanging Spells into the Vicissitude section on them, so hopefully that will help clear up that confusion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T19:25:33-07:00","id":195945,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I'll check that out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T13:07:14-08:00","id":821153,"title":"","content":"In light of a number of different write ups about the Tzimisce proliferating, I kinda want to bring this one back under scrutiny.<br /> <br /> I've struck through the section on Vicissitude as I think I need to come back to that and attempt something more original and simple on how to implement it. I have a few ideas vis-a-vis weird things like the Equipment system, but nothing concrete again.<br /> <br /> Just to reiterate, I didn't really have any sacred cows from the Masquerade version beyond a desire for them to have fleshcrafting, so there's a lot of baggage from the Tzimisce of Masquerade that's cut completely from this bloodline.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd love it if people would read for thematic consistency between their history and character, with an eye directed towards how the Bloodline Gift/Bane play into that. Thoughts on how well they work as a Ventrue bloodline also helps, as I remember reading the suggestion that a Bloodline should further refine a clan concept and I definitely tried to do that here.<br /> <br /> I know this is also a very basic question, but strictly speaking, do you find these guys interesting? If so, what makes them interesting to you? If not, where do you think it falls apart? What changes might you suggest to make them more towards your tastes? I'm very interested in people's ideas about how to make these guys both interesting as NPCs and as PCs.<br /> <br /> And this is just a fun little one: If there are places where you think more fun easter eggs referencing the original Tzimisce might fit in there, I'm all ears!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:45:50-08:00","id":822562,"title":"","content":"Given that I was the original designer of the system you are now junking, I am probably exempt from having to provide commentary. But I've a few minutes till I finish work, so you get random philosophizing. I will say that there is something fascinating about the way that Tzimisce and Vicissitude have caught the fanbase's imagination and <i>will not let go</i>. A quick glance at the Homebrew Hub shows nearly half a dozen variants of these guys. <br /> <br /> From a mechanical perspective, Vicissitude is a bloody nightmare (and not in a good way). Basically, my perspective is that there tends to be a kind of three-cornered tug-of-war between Versatility, Simplicity, and Balance -- you can have any two. Versatile powers can do a lot of things, so you either need to spend a lot of word count setting limits, or risk having that power become a kind of &quot;and this is all you need&quot; ability. If you have a strict limit to your word count, then you can either spend it describing all the stuff the power <i>can</i> do (versatility), or all the stuff it can't do (balance), but probably not both. If you want to keep your powerset balanced, then you need to devote extra word count to clearly delineate what it can and cannot do, which means that you either sacrifice what the power <i>can</i> do in order to keep your explanations concise, or you end up with long lists of what can or cannot be done. <br /> <br /> This isn't <i>quite</i> a zero sum game -- good writing can mitigate things to some extent -- but in my experience one of the three tends to suffer. My blood sorcery system emphasized versatility and balance, but yes, it was a bloody long thing.<br /> <br /> As for what's interesting or not... I personally feel like slaughtering sacred cows is the wrong approach, because the sacred cows are what make the Tzimisce interesting. In other words, like a lot of Masquerade clans, the Tzimisce were a ludicrously cobbled together mixture of a dozen different ideas, but more than most of the others for them that approach <i>worked</i>. They got Dracula+Flesh Crafting+EEEEEEVIL, and it seems to have hooked into the fandom's psyche in a really strong way. If you strip out much of that, what's left is... eh? Not bad, but nothing to grab the imagination in quite the same way.<br /> <br /> That said, I also think that in NWoD, the Ordo Dracul has inherited a lot of the Dracula/Mad Scientist vibe from the Tzimisce (and the Dragons are regularly called the most popular covenant, coincidence?). So what might be interesting would be to, instead of making the Tzimisce a Bloodline, work them up as a variation on the Ordo Dracul. A set of traditions and powers, perhaps with Vicissitude being a Mystery and attendant Scales.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T14:19:51-08:00","id":822751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=822562#post822562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that I was the original designer of the system you are now junking, I am probably exempt from having to provide commentary. But I've a few minutes till I finish work, so you get random philosophizing. I will say that there is something fascinating about the way that Tzimisce and Vicissitude have caught the fanbase's imagination and <i>will not let go</i>. A quick glance at the Homebrew Hub shows nearly half a dozen variants of these guys.<br /> <br /> From a mechanical perspective, Vicissitude is a bloody nightmare (and not in a good way). Basically, my perspective is that there tends to be a kind of three-cornered tug-of-war between Versatility, Simplicity, and Balance -- you can have any two. Versatile powers can do a lot of things, so you either need to spend a lot of word count setting limits, or risk having that power become a kind of &quot;and this is all you need&quot; ability. If you have a strict limit to your word count, then you can either spend it describing all the stuff the power <i>can</i> do (versatility), or all the stuff it can't do (balance), but probably not both. If you want to keep your powerset balanced, then you need to devote extra word count to clearly delineate what it can and cannot do, which means that you either sacrifice what the power <i>can</i> do in order to keep your explanations concise, or you end up with long lists of what can or cannot be done.<br /> <br /> <br /> This isn't <i>quite</i> a zero sum game -- good writing can mitigate things to some extent -- but in my experience one of the three tends to suffer. My blood sorcery system emphasized versatility and balance, but yes, it was a bloody long thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved your take on Vicissitude and I still like it! I'm just trying to consider alternatives both because of general misgivings I have about Extended Actions and thus the Blood Sorcery rules, and a desire to make my homebrew feel a bit less dependant. Basically I sort of feel bad using your work like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=822562#post822562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what's interesting or not... I personally feel like slaughtering sacred cows is the wrong approach, because the sacred cows are what make the Tzimisce interesting. In other words, like a lot of Masquerade clans, the Tzimisce were a ludicrously cobbled together mixture of a dozen different ideas, but more than most of the others for them that approach <i>worked</i>. They got Dracula+Flesh Crafting+EEEEEEVIL, and it seems to have hooked into the fandom's psyche in a really strong way. If you strip out much of that, what's left is... eh? Not bad, but nothing to grab the imagination in quite the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a great way of summing up the Masquerade clans. I have to admit that the fleshcrafting is really the only part of them that I liked, and that's probably showing. I think the power and the possibility of relating it to the Ventrue via a concept of dominating flesh was the best way to reflect it, so that probably shows. It might be that I should separate this from the Tzimisce by changing the name. I'll have to think on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=822562#post822562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I also think that in NWoD, the Ordo Dracul has inherited a lot of the Dracula/Mad Scientist vibe from the Tzimisce (and the Dragons are regularly called the most popular covenant, coincidence?). So what might be interesting would be to, instead of making the Tzimisce a Bloodline, work them up as a variation on the Ordo Dracul. A set of traditions and powers, perhaps with Vicissitude being a Mystery and attendant Scales.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fascinating idea. How would one make it into a Mystery? You'd have to find a part of the Kindred template that it might interact with. The thing that comes to mind is how Kindred's bodies heal wounds, requiring a Willpower to not heal them/not return your features to what they were when you were Embraced. If one were to take it in that direction, I imagine it'd be about modifying the body, maybe changing one's flesh to look like another and other such things, all in service of becoming a perfect predator. Maybe the Scales are how they do it to other creatures.<br /> <br /> That makes Vicissitude maybe less of a power and more of a procedure, but it's an interesting idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 02-03-2016, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T17:44:01-08:00","id":822914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=822751#post822751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I loved your take on Vicissitude and I still like it! I'm just trying to consider alternatives both because of general misgivings I have about Extended Actions and thus the Blood Sorcery rules, and a desire to make my homebrew feel a bit less dependant. Basically I sort of feel bad using your work like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>*snort* You needn't feel bad about <i>that</i>. It's intensely flattering to have other people think my stuff is worth working off of!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/189183-the-tzimisce-a-ventrue-bloodline?p=822751#post822751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fascinating idea. How would one make it into a Mystery? You'd have to find a part of the Kindred template that it might interact with. The thing that comes to mind is how Kindred's bodies heal wounds, requiring a Willpower to not heal them/not return your features to what they were when you were Embraced. If one were to take it in that direction, I imagine it'd be about modifying the body, maybe changing one's flesh to look like another and other such things, all in service of becoming a perfect predator. Maybe the Scales are how they do it to other creatures.<br /> <br /> That makes Vicissitude maybe less of a power and more of a procedure, but it's an interesting idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess Mysteries are a weak area for me -- B&amp;S came around after I'd already invested a LOT of game time into the Coils, so we just updated those and didn't convert the system. That said, the thought which occurs to me is the fact that Kindred have a unique relationship of unliving flesh and living blood. In other words, a large part of a vampire's physical body is inert. It's why they're bullet-proof, because if a bullet punctures a vampire's lung... eh? So what? On the other hand, vampiric Vitae is <i>more </i>active than blood. Yet given this weird setup, there's nothing that says a vampire's body has to be in a standard shape. So long as it's got Vitae flowing through it, it'll run.<br /> <br /> I think that a Mystery of Vicissitude would take this idea and use it to counter that aspect of the Curse which requires vampiric bodies to stay in stasis. I can see some 'positive' side-effects in the idea that Vicissitude can allow a vampire to simulate aging, or fix certain pre-mortem disabilities, and so forth. But from a Vitae-Science approach, it's a short jump from &quot;adding wrinkles to your skin&quot; to &quot;adding knives to your fingers.&quot; Using Scales to allow you to inject Vitae into others to work its transformative magic seems eminently reasonable.<br /> <br /> In other words... the Bane of Stasis locks vampires into the moment of their death. The Mystery of Vicissitude reclaims for the Kindred the ability to grow, change, and mutilate their bodies however <i>they</i> want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}